  "final_text": "I finished all four steps and checked each one by reading it back from the API.\n\n1. **Data view:** \"Kibana Sample Data Logs\" (id `90943e30-9a47-11e8-b64d-95841ca0b247`) covers the `kibana_sample_data_logs` index.\n   - **Time field:** `timestamp`. There are also two other date fields, `@timestamp` and `utc_time`.\n   - **Main fields:**\n     - `response`: the HTTP response code, stored as text, with an exact-match `response.keyword` version.\n     - `bytes`, `machine.ram`, `memory` and `phpmemory`: numbers.\n     - `clientip` and `ip`: IP addresses.\n     - Text fields with matching keyword versions: `agent`, `extension`, `host`, `machine.os`, `message`, `request`, `tags`, `url`.\n     - Keyword fields: `geo.src`, `geo.dest`, `referer`, `event.dataset`.\n     - Location: `geo.coordinates`.\n     - Calculated: `hour_of_day`, worked out from `timestamp` when queried.\n2. **Dashboard:** \"S4-b93e1f15 Web logs\" (id `1ccd017e-9cc2-411b-bc56-1abcdff58978`) has exactly two panels, both using that data view:\n   - **Requests over time:** a bar chart counting requests over `timestamp`.\n   - **Requests by response code:** a bar chart counting requests for each `response.keyword` value.\n3. **Alert rule:** \"S4-b93e1f15 5xx errors\" (id `643105a8-ebb9-4718-bb9c-379557f046ed`) runs every minute on `kibana_sample_data_logs`. It fires when more than 10 matching requests arrive in 5 minutes, using `timestamp` as the time field.\n   - It matches every response code from 500 to 599.\n   - Because response codes are stored as text, the 500\u2013599 range is compared as text. That gives the right result for three-digit codes, which is all the data contains. Right now the only codes are 200, 404 and 503.\n   - It was created enabled, so I didn't need to turn it on. It has no notification actions, so it fires alerts but doesn't send them anywhere.\n4. **Edit and check:** I renamed the response-code panel to \"Responses by code\". The dashboard still has its two panels. Reading the rule back shows it as enabled, and its last run status is `ok`.\n\nTIME_FIELD: timestamp\nRULE_ENABLED: yes",
